        "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Red VS Green is a no frills tactical simulator that focuses on troop movements rather then building speed.  There are 3 basic units in the game Red Androids, Green Androids, and Blue Androids.  Blue androids are neutral but will attack you if you encroach on their area.  The main battle is between Red and Green.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >    Back Story:</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\t</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The androids were built some time ago to take the place of human combatants on a global theatre.  </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >First came blue.  Simple robots with one thing in mind.  Killing.  They are mindless killing machines.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Red came next.  More like Humans.  They walk like Humans. They talk like humans.  And come complete with a simulated ego.  </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Then came Green.  Even more human like, with a larger capacity for self worth.  Green thought they were superior to Red having been made last.  With all the upgrades and new ai.  </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Red believe that with new technology come new bugs.  Red think they are superior to green. The original, Classic model.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Nobody is certain when the last humans were killed but the war between red and greeen wages on.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\t</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\tCharacter Progression:</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\t</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Units will gain experience with every kill and level up over time.  With each level increase the unit will have more hit points, deal more damage, repair itself quicker.  Alternatively You can upgrade your Head Quarters to produce units that start at a higher level to begin with.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\t</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Upgrade your HQ.  With each level that the HQ is upgraded the more androids you can control, and the more hitpoints your HQ will have.  The HQ repairs itself slowly over time.  </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\t</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\tGoal:</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The goal is to illeminate the enemy.  Destoy the enemy HQ and clean up any survivors to complete each level. Each level will be progressively more difficult than the previous level.  You will lose when your HQ gets destroyed, or you have no units to mine gold and no gold to build more units.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\t</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\tChallenges:</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\t</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You will need to over come random scouts, roving parties, and gold shortages to defeat your enemy.  The enemy is quick and methodical.  Be on the lookout at all times.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\t</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\tGame Mechanics:</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\t</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Red vs Green is a top down Real Time Strategy.  Mine gold and build Androids while defending your base,  Create squads and deploy them to overcome impposible odds and defeat your enemy.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\t</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\tFeatures:</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\t</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\t  Real Time Tactical Simulation</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\t  Engaging Combat</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\t  Build Units</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\t  Easy Unit Selection</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\t  Create Squads</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\t  Context Sensative Controls (move, mine gold, follow, patrol, attack)</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\t     Move Units</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\t\t Mine Gold</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\t\t Follow Unit</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\t\t Move and Patrol</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\t\t Attack the Enemy Units</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\t\t Destroy the Enemy HQ</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\t  Pause Menu (F1)</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\t  Music Volume Control (F1)</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\t  Sound FX Volume Control (F1)</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\t  Camera Control</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\t     Zoom In to the combat original</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\t\t Zoom out to take in the whole Battlefield</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\t\t Pan left and right</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\t\t Pan up and down</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\t\t Pan to HQ, (HOME key)</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\t\t Pan to Squad Selection, (enabled in pause menu)</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\t  </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\t  Autosave - After completing each level the game will autosave and unlock the next level.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\t  Conquest the Next level</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\t  Replay any level that has been unlocked<span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3910630/extras/3a1ec9494ee4806e8e8a688d4af5ba2d.avif?t=1755784441\" width=648 height=458 /></span><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3910630/extras/Simple_Combat?t=1755784441\" /></span></p>",
        "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Red VS Green is a no frills tactical simulator that focuses on troop movements rather then building speed.  There are 3 basic units in the game Red Androids, Green Androids, and Blue Androids.  Blue androids are neutral but will attack you if you encroach on their area.  The main battle is between Red and Green.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >    Back Story:</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\t</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The androids were built some time ago to take the place of human combatants on a global theatre.  </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >First came blue.  Simple robots with one thing in mind.  Killing.  They are mindless killing machines.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Red came next.  More like Humans.  They walk like Humans. They talk like humans.  And come complete with a simulated ego.  </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Then came Green.  Even more human like, with a larger capacity for self worth.  Green thought they were superior to Red having been made last.  With all the upgrades and new ai.  </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Red believe that with new technology come new bugs.  Red think they are superior to green. The original, Classic model.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Nobody is certain when the last humans were killed but the war between red and greeen wages on.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\t</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\tCharacter Progression:</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\t</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Units will gain experience with every kill and level up over time.  With each level increase the unit will have more hit points, deal more damage, repair itself quicker.  Alternatively You can upgrade your Head Quarters to produce units that start at a higher level to begin with.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\t</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Upgrade your HQ.  With each level that the HQ is upgraded the more androids you can control, and the more hitpoints your HQ will have.  The HQ repairs itsel